		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=5398#p5398"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>quelque chose de trouvé <br />je fait ma requete&#160; par tranche de code postal <br />mais a chaque fois je suis obligé de faire&#160; vacuum analyse sinon ca plante <br />d&#039;ou ca vient ?</p><p>Configuration dans postgres.conf --&gt; Gleu merci de me repondre </p><br /><p>vacuum analyse cadastre.infoparc;<br />vacuum analyse pos.pos_hist;</p><p>update&#160; cadastre.infoparc as a set <br />gen_niv2_06 =&#160; b.gen_niv2,<br />an_aprob_06 = b.an_aprob, <br />chg_ap2002 = b.chg_ap2002<br />from pos.pos_hist as b<br />where&#160; b.anneeval = &#039;2006&#039; <br />and (a.the_geom &amp;&amp; b.the_geom)<br />AND intersects(a.the_geom, b.the_geom)<br />and a.id_insee=b.id_insee<br />and substr(a.id_insee,1,2)=&#039;84&#039;<br />and substr(b.id_insee,1,2)=&#039;84&#039;<br />and a.id_insee between &#039;84021&#039; and &#039;84050&#039;<br />and a.the_geom is not null<br />and b.the_geom is not null;</p>]]></content>
